# File: tests/features/status-snapshot.feature
# Generated from: specs/43-publish-the-selected-routed-model-s-plan-usage-for-a-custom-statusline-command/requirements.md
Feature: Publish the selected routed model's plan usage for a custom statusLine command

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A routed step publishes the selected provider's windows
    Given an OpenCode Go model is selected and its usage reading reports 5h, weekly and monthly windows
    When a routed main-loop step completes
    Then the session's snapshot under ~/.claude/nmg-router/status names opencode-go, the model and those three windows in order

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A reading that arrives later updates the snapshot
    Given an OpenCode Go step's snapshot was written before its usage read finished
    When the read finishes while OpenCode Go is still shown without an error
    Then the snapshot is rewritten with the new windows

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Switching providers never shows the earlier provider's windows
    Given the snapshot shows OpenCode Go's windows and an OpenCode Go usage read is still running
    When an xAI main-loop step completes and the OpenCode Go read then finishes
    Then the snapshot names xai and its model with no windows

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Errors and Claude steps clear the windows
    Given the snapshot shows OpenCode Go's windows
    When a routed main-loop step fails, and later a Claude main-loop step runs
    Then the failed step's snapshot has no windows, and the Claude step's snapshot has no provider, model or windows

  @SCN005
  Scenario: The snapshot never affects the routed step
    Given writing the snapshot fails
    When a routed main-loop step completes
    Then the step's answer and the status line are unchanged and no error is shown

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The snapshot holds no secret and only valid session ids name a file
    Given a routed step with a sentinel credential
    When the snapshot is written on Linux
    Then it holds no credential, the file is 0600 in a 0700 directory and replaced atomically, and a session id "../x" writes no file

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Subagent steps leave the snapshot alone
    Given a snapshot for the main loop
    When a routed subagent step completes
    Then the snapshot is not rewritten
